-- title:
--   Connected–étale splitting in Hopf form over p-adically complete 𝒪
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, let $\mathbb Z/p$ carry an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure whose structure map has kernel exactly the ideal $(p)$, and assume $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for $(p)$. Let $L$ be a commutative ring which is a cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module with $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O} L = p^N$, and let $R_0$ be a commutative ring which is a Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, free and finite over $\mathcal O$ and a local ring. Let $\rho \colon L \to R_0$ be a surjective morphism of $\mathcal O$-bialgebras whose kernel, as an ideal of $L$, equals $(1-e)$ for an idempotent $e \in L$ with $\varepsilon(e)=1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a commutative ring $H$ carrying a cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra structure, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module and formally étale over $\mathcal O$, together with a morphism of $\mathcal O$-bialgebras $j \colon H \to L$ such that: $\ker \rho$ equals the ideal of $L$ generated by the image under $j$ of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon_H)$; the ring map underlying $j$ is faithfully flat and finite; $j$ is injective; $R_0$ is cocommutative; and $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O} R_0 = p^{a}$ for some natural number $a$.
--
--   This is the connected–étale exact sequence $0 \to G^{0} \to G \to G^{\mathrm{\acute et}} \to 0$ of a finite flat commutative group scheme over a $p$-adically complete base, written in Hopf-algebra terms: $H = \mathcal O(G^{\mathrm{\acute et}})$, the ring map $j$ realises $L$ as finite faithfully flat over $H$, and the connected component $\operatorname{Spec} R_0$ is cut out by the augmentation ideal of $H$. It is used in the dévissage step [`Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp).
